    kg:textSpan "UMAP (McInnes et al., 2018) to project them to a two dimensional space. Figure 5 reveals the relationship between number of cancer cells in the breast cancer tissue and regions of the latent space, low counts of cancer cells (class 0) are concentrated at quadrant II while they increase as we move to quadrant IV (class 7). Figure 6 displays how the distinct regions of the latent space generate dierent kinds of tissue. These examples provide evidence of a structured latent space according to tissu" .

