    kg:textSpan "probabilistic models (DDPMs) [ 29 ], [ 23 ] have emerged as a new set of generative models for image synthesis. DDPMs are a collection of generative models that produce high-quality images through iterative denoising. In contrast to GANs, diffusion models exhibit more stable training and produce higher-quality images [ 23 ]. Furthermore, Rombach et al . [ 22 ] enhanced diffusion models speed and performance by introducing a latent diffusion model (LDM) that operates in variational autoencoder (V" .

