    kg:textSpan "of the proposed StainFuser. StainFuser takes in a source and target image to predict the stain normalized version of the source image. The application of StainFuser was demonstrated through a nuclei segmentation and classification task and a WSI-level inference task. and obtain Z = { z 1 , z 2 , ..., z n } . For curating the target set T , we perform k-means clustering on Z and obtain a set of 512 clusters C = { c 1 , c 2 , ..., c 512 } . To select the most representative patch of each cluster, " .

