    kg:textSpan ")] + KL [ q ( z | X, Y ) , p ( z )]) + ( where controls the impact of L Align . (9) where q ( z | X, Y ) represents the joint posterior of the pathological and genomic features. For the purpose of computing log p ( x i | z i , Y ) , we additionally incorporate the latent representation z Y into the reconstruction network i . 3.7. Multimodal Fusion and Prediction After obtaining the pathological features Y and the reconstruction genomic features X from the LD-CVAE, we combine them to obtain the f" .

<http://example.org/kg/chunk/2503_09496_rag__chunk_012> a kg:Chunk ;
    kg:chunkId "2503.09496_rag::chunk_012" ;
    kg:docId "2503.09496_rag" ;
    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/2503_09496_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "97,608 89,498 pixels 5. Conclusion Figure 5. Comparison of the co-attention weights calculated from the genuine (top) and generated (bottom) genomic features. In this paper, we present a Conditional Latent Differentiation Variational AutoEncoder (LD-CVAE) that can reconstruct the genomic embeddings with diverse biological functions from WSIs for robust multimodal survival prediction. The experimental results on five different cancer datasets demonstrate the superiority of our method under both c" .

