    kg:textSpan "range of applications, including synthetic data generation, stain normalization, style transfer, tissue synthesis, and rare pathology simulation, thereby enhancing learning-based approaches under data-scarce or domain-shifted conditions. Research on content generation models in pathology has grown rapidly, as illustrated in Fig. 2 . After a period of sparse, exploratory studies, publication volume increased steadily, with a sharp rise from 2024 onward. This inflection point marks a broader shift" .

