    kg:textSpan "224 224 pixel image tiles at a 20 magnification level, corresponding to a resolution of 0.5 m/pixel. Tiles with at least 25% tissue by area are used during training and the rest are discarded. To estimate the amount of tissue in a tile, each WSI is downsampled 16 with bilinear interpolation and every pixel of the downsampled image is evaluated as to whether its hue, saturation, and value are within [90, 180], [8, 255], and [103, 255], respectively. These tiles are subsequently processed with Vir" .

