    kg:textSpan "35 ]. These limitations are amplified in spatial omics, where cellular identity and state are determined not only by intrinsic features but also by neighboring cells and broader tissue architecture. Existing models fall short in integrating spatial, molecular, and morphological information at single-cell resolution. Single-cell foundation models focus on transcriptomics and ignore morphology entirely [ 11 , 28 ] or focus on spot-level spatial correlations [ 58 , 59 , 65 , 49 , 34 ]. Pathology mo" .

