    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/1907_02644_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "Adversarial Networks (GANs) have become increasingly popular, applied to dierent domains from imaging to signal processing. GANs (Goodfellow et al., 2014) are able to learn high delity and diverse data representations from a target distribution. This is done with a generator, G ( z ), that maps random noise, z p z ( z ), to samples that resemble the target data, x p data ( x ), and a discriminator, D ( x ), whose goal is to distinguish between real and generated samples. The goal of a GAN is nd " .

