    :hasEvidenceText "By generating histology images conditioned on molecular profiles, these models provide visual hypotheses"^^xsd:string,
        "By generating histology images conditioned on molecular profiles, these models provide visual hypotheses for how molecular states shape tissue architecture"^^xsd:string,
        "Content generation models in computational pathology have undergone a rapid evolution over the past decade"^^xsd:string,
        "Content generation models in computational pathology have undergone a rapid evolution over the past decade, marked by successive paradigm shifts driven by architectural breakthroughs."^^xsd:string,
        "DDPMs are a collection of generative models that produce high-quality images through iterative denoising."^^xsd:string,
        "Diffusion models adopt masked denoising [16], further enhanced by Transformerbased context modeling [51] and latent-space optimization [107]"^^xsd:string,
        "GANs (Goodfellow et al., 2014) are able to learn high delity and diverse data representations from a target distribution."^^xsd:string,
        "Generative artificial intelligence is increasingly reshaping computational pathology"^^xsd:string,
        "Generative artificial intelligence is increasingly reshaping computational pathology, impacting diagnostic imaging, knowledge extraction, and clinical decision-making."^^xsd:string,
        "Generative models are trained to approximate data distributions"^^xsd:string,
        "Generative models are trained to approximate data distributions rather than to establish verifiable inputoutput mappings"^^xsd:string,
        "PathologyGAN The Frechet Inception Distance (FID) (Heusel et al., 2017) is a common metric used to measure GANs performance"^^xsd:string,
        "PathologyGAN does reproduce these distributions not only when it is judged by convolutional features (32 . 05 / 16 . 65) but also when we use an external tool to directly quantify cellular information"^^xsd:string,
        "Realistic data enrichment from masks for robust segmentation."^^xsd:string,
        "Recent generative models have significantly advanced synthetic pathology imaging"^^xsd:string,
        "Recent generative models have significantly advanced synthetic pathology imaging, addressing challenges such as limited annotations, class imbalance, and domain shifts."^^xsd:string,
        "The flexibility of diffusion models has also facilitated unified, multi-task architectures capable of any-to-any stain conversion"^^xsd:string,
        "The model is capable of generating text-based diagnosis reports for WSIs."^^xsd:string,
        "The translation of generative models into clinical practice is constrained by systemic barriers"^^xsd:string,
        "These comparisons highlight the steep escalation in training costs as models progress from lightweight GANs to diffusion and foundation-scale architectures."^^xsd:string,
        "Utilizing generative models to create in-silico data"^^xsd:string,
        "demonstrates the capability of our pre-trained model to generate histology slices"^^xsd:string,
        "enabling the generator to generate images that are similar to the real images in the target domain"^^xsd:string,
        "generative cell simulation offers a targeted means of alleviating annotation bottlenecks in biomedical imaging by producing synthetic datasets"^^xsd:string,
        "models progress from lightweight GANs to diffusion and foundation-scale architectures."^^xsd:string,
        "our review is centered on content generation models as a distinct methodological paradigm."^^xsd:string,
        "training costs as models progress from lightweight GANs to diffusion and foundation-scale architectures."^^xsd:string ;
    rdfs:subClassOf :entity,
        owl:Thing ;
    skos:altLabel "GenerativeModel"^^xsd:string ;
    skos:skos_definition "Models in computational pathology that have undergone evolution for content generation, including architectural breakthroughs for synthesizing images."^^xsd:string ;
